<title>USA: W. Memphis, Ark., $18 mln priced, 5.25 pct top yld.</title>
<headline>W. Memphis, Ark., $18 mln priced, 5.25 pct top yld.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Chicago Capital Markets Inc said Monday it tentatively priced $18 million of West Memphis, Ark., public utility system refunding revenue bonds, 1996 Series A, with a top yield of 5.25 in 2008.</p>
<p>The bonds are MBIA insured.  </p>
<p>CITY OF WEST MEMPHIS, ARKANSAS</p>
<p>RE: $17,660,000*</p>
<p>PUBLIC UTILITY SYSTEM REFUNDING REVENUE BONDS</p>
<p>1996 SERIES A</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aaa		   S&amp;P: NR</p>
<p>MBIA INSURED</p>
<p>DATED: 11/01/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 06/01/1997</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p> MATURITY		AMOUNT*    COUPON	   PRICE</p>
